CORE
function_access.c
--function f --pointer-check
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[precondition_instance\.1\] .*static array parameter x must provide access to its declared minimum: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The --function harness substitutes both earlier arguments into the outer
static minimum and the inner runtime dimension, so the last promised element
is accessible. The access goes through a flat element pointer because
symbolic indexing of a multidimensional variable-length array hits an existing
goto-symex limitation that this feature does not address.
